\p
\v 16 I'll say¦124567 it again: no¦124568 one should suppose¦124571 that I'm foolish, but¦124575 if they do, at least accept me as¦124580 foolish so that I can also¦124585 boast¦124589 a little¦124586.
\v 17 When I say that¦124602, I'm not¦124592 talking¦124591 \add words from\add* \nd Yahweh¦124595\nd*, but¦124597 like a fool confidently¦124604 boasting¦124606.
\v 18 Many¦124608 boast like worldly \add people\add*, so I'll¦124613 boast as well,
\v 19 because¦124616 you¦124617 prudent¦124620 \add ones\add* happily tolerate¦124617 foolish¦124619 people.
\v 20 Yes, you tolerate¦124622 those who'll enslave¦124627 you all, those who'll exploit you, those who'll take¦124633 \add advantage of\add* you all, those who promote themselves, and anyone whacks you in¦124640 the¦124641 face¦124641.
\v 21 I'm talking¦124660 about dishonour¦124645 as¦124647 if we¦124649 were weak, but¦124654 (speaking¦124660 foolishly¦124659 again), anything that¦124648 anyone¦124656 else is brave enough to do, then I will also be brave enough \add to match\add*.
\v 22 Are they Hebrews? I am too. Are they Israelis? So am I. Are they descendants of Abraham¦124670? Me also.
\v 23 Are¦124675 they¦124675 Messiah's servants? \add Well,\add* I'm above¦124678 them¦124678 (speaking¦124677 insanely¦124676 now): I've worked harder, been in¦124680 prison¦124687 more often, \add endured\add* uncountable beatings¦124691, and been close to death¦124695 more often.\x + \xo 11:23: \xt Acts 16:23.\x*
\v 24 I've received¦124703 the thirty-nine lashes from the Jewish \add leadership\add* five¦124699 times¦124699,\x + \xo 11:24: \xt Deu 25:3.\x*
\v 25 was beaten¦124705 three times with¦124705 rods¦124705, was stoned¦124707 once¦124706, shipwrecked¦124709 three times, and I was in¦124711 the¦124712 ocean for a day¦124710 and a night¦124710.\x + \xo 11:25: a \xt Acts 16:22; \xo b \xt Acts 14:19.\x*
\v 26 I've done \add many long\add* trips, crossed dangerous rivers¦124718, risked being robbed¦124720, \add was persecuted\add* by my own people as well as by non-Jews, have been in danger in the city¦124729, in the wilderness¦124732 and on¦124734 the ocean, \add as well as being attacked\add* by false¦124738 \add teachers\add*.\x + \xo 11:26: a \xt Acts 9:23; \xo b \xt Acts 14:5.\x*
\v 27 I've worked often and worked hard, often needing to keep guard, \add suffered\add* famine¦124747 and thirst¦124749, fasted often, and been cold¦124754 and lacking clothing.
\v 28 \add Then\add* apart from¦124757 all those external¦124759 things, I've been opposed every day¦124767—\add not to mention\add* my concern for all the¦124771 assemblies¦124772.
\v 29 What person falters and I don't falter with them? Who stumbles¦124779 \add in their walk with God\add* and I don't suffer with them?
\p
\v 30 If it's appropriate¦124786 to¦124785 be boasting¦124785, what I'd boast about would be my¦124790 weaknesses¦124789.
