\v 4 was¦124905 pulled \add up\add* into paradise¦124908 and¦124909 heard¦124910 messages¦124912 which¦124913 can't¦124914 be put into words (because \add living\add* people aren't¦124914 allow to speak¦124917 them).
\v 5 I'm \add prepared\add* to boast about that man¦124920, but¦124923 I won't boast about myself¦124924 because I won't boast \add at all\add* except¦124928 \add about\add* my¦124931 weaknesses¦124932,
\v 6 because even if¦124934 I did want¦124936 to¦124938 boast¦124938, I wouldn't be being foolish¦124942, because I would be speaking¦124945 the truth¦124943. But¦124947 I'll¦124941 refrain¦124946 in case anyone¦124949 reckons that I'm more than what they can see¦124955 or¦124957 hear¦124958 about me¦124961.
\p
\v 7 So¦124962 to keep my head from getting too big because of those incredible revelations¦124966, I was given¦124971 a ‘thorn¦124973’ in my body¦124975—Satan's¦124977 messenger¦124976 to harass me and¦124962 keep me from becoming conceited.
\v 8 Three times I begged the¦124988 \nd master¦124989\nd* that¦124986 it might leave me¦124994
\v 9 and¦124995 he¦124996 told me, “Is my grace¦125001 good enough for you¦124999? \add My\add* power reaches its conclusion through weakness¦125008.” Therefore¦125012 I'll¦125014 quite gladly¦125011 boast¦125014 about my weaknesses¦125017 so that the \nd messiah's¦125026\nd* power can take¦125020 residence¦125020 in me.
\v 10 So¦125027 then I take¦125028 pleasure¦125028 in weaknesses¦125030, in insults¦125032 and hardships¦125035, in persecutions¦125037 and distresses¦125040 for \nd Messiah¦125042\nd* because¦125044 whenever¦125043 I might be¦125045 faltering¦125045, that's when I'm powerful¦125047.
